  "security_implications": "This chunk aggregates multiple hardware error indicators (counter, state, sparse FSM, control integrity) into combined status signals and feeds them to a hardware interrupt provider. If any error aggregation or the interrupt path fails (e.g., missing an input, propagating X, or mis‑connecting event_error), the system may operate in a faulted state without raising an alert. This can directly violate security goals that depend on timely detection of integrity violations, such as those from SHA‑3 counters, KMAC state machines, or control storage. Ensuring that all constituent error sources are correctly generated and that the OR‑based aggregation and interrupt instance function properly is essential for safety monitoring.",
